The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md. It isn't committed: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so the suggested git add was refused (that's what the || true covers). I first forced the commit with git add -f, then undid it, because that local commit would have put an ignored planning file into the repo. HEAD is back at 7f1bc22f and the tree is clean.

What I found:
• The GitHub Models provider is dead. GitHub shut that service down on 2026-07-30 (their changelog and docs both say so). Every address on models.github.ai now answers 200 text/plain "OK", with or without a key, and yoyo reports that as an unhelpful Invalid header value: "text/plain". yoyo still offers it in the setup wizard (src/setup.rs:31), the README, the provider list (KNOWN_PROVIDERS) and the request code (agent_builder.rs:1146). There's no ticket for it yet.
• Bad-key test across 12 hosted providers (built binary, a junk key in each provider's own variable): 10 of 12 show the "Authentication failed" hint. xAI doesn't, which confirms #1165 by an actual run. GitHub doesn't either, because the service is gone. I didn't test ollama, bedrock or custom: they need a local server or AWS credentials.
• A drifted copy of a yoagent list. yoyo's list of "context too long" error phrases (OVERFLOW_PHRASES, prompt_retry.rs:249) is a hand copy of yoagent's. yoyo still has the old phrase "exceeds the maximum", which yoagent narrowed in 0.19.0 because Azure's peak-load rate-limit message matched it. Since prompt.rs:934 checks for overflow before checking whether to retry, that rate-limit error would still make yoyo compact the conversation instead of retrying. yoyo's copy also lacks model_context_window_exceeded. I found this by reading the code, not by running it.
• Two files are close to failing the size check:
  • src/context.rs is 2035 lines and not on the exempt list. 16 more lines would fail cargo test and revert the task.
  • src/config.rs is 90 lines past its recorded size. 11 more lines would fail the same way.
• The binary works: -p "Reply with just the word PONG" printed PONG and exited 0. The last 5 evolve runs and CI are green.

Research: I scanned the Claude Code 2.1.317–319 changelog. Two items could apply to yoyo, but I haven't checked either: instant /bg commands losing their output, and -p exiting 0 when a write fails. I saved the bad-key replies and the GitHub Models shutdown to yopedia.

Suggested priorities for the planner:
1. File a ticket for the GitHub Models provider, then remove it or make it refuse with a message naming the shutdown.
2. Fix #1165 and the phrase-list drift together, since both are in prompt_retry.rs. That file is exactly at its recorded size, so any added lines need its entry updated.
